.TH SEMVER-FORGE 1 "2026-11-04" "semver-forge 1.2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
semver-forge \- automatic semantic version tracking and synchronization
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B semver-forge
.RI [ global-options ]
.I command
.RI [ command-options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B semver-forge
manages a project's semantic version. It selects a canonical version source, calculates version increments from Git history, and synchronizes configured version metadata.
.PP
Normal output is intentionally concise. Use
.B --verbose
for expanded operation details and
.B --debug
for troubleshooting diagnostics and tracebacks.
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
.TP
.B --project DIR
Operate on the specified project directory. Defaults to the current directory.
.TP
.B --json
Emit machine-readable JSON.
.TP
.B --verbose
Show expanded operation reports, including discovery results, synchronization details, and configuration scope information.
.TP
.B --debug
Enable expanded diagnostic output and print Python tracebacks for caught operation errors. Debug mode includes verbose information.
.TP
.B --version
Print the installed SemVer Forge version.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B init [--yes]
Inspect project metadata and create
.I .semver-forge.toml
with the canonical version source and synchronization targets. Existing recognized version values are preserved. If recognized sources disagree, initialization stops and reports the conflict. If no usable version source exists, initialization creates a root
.I VERSION
file and uses it as the authority.
.IP
If configuration already exists, initialization asks before replacing it. Use
.B --yes
to authorize replacement without the prompt.
.TP
.B next [--dry-run] [--explain]
Inspect Git commits since the last processed commit boundary and select the highest configured semantic-version impact. Breaking changes select MAJOR, features select MINOR, and fixes/performance changes select PATCH by default. The selected version is written to the canonical source and configured synchronization targets when a bump is warranted. The processed Git boundary is saved so the same commits are not counted again.
.IP
.B --dry-run
previews the decision without writing. 
.B --explain
includes the reason for the selected version or no-change decision.
.TP
.B sync [--dry-run] [--discover] [--version VERSION]
Write the canonical version to every configured synchronization target.
.B --dry-run
previews file changes without writing.
.B --discover
recursively searches for supported version metadata, adds newly discovered targets to the project
.I [sync].targets
configuration, and synchronizes them. The operation is idempotent: existing targets are not duplicated.
.B --version VERSION
uses the supplied version for this synchronization instead of reading the canonical version.
.TP
.B check [--verbose] [--debug]
Print the project name, canonical version, and synchronized file paths. The command is read-only. Verbose mode includes canonical-source validation, target values and statuses, discovered metadata, and configuration diagnostics.
.TP
.B config [OPTIONS] [get KEY | set KEY TOML_VALUE | unset KEY]
Inspect and manage SemVer Forge configuration.
.IP
With no action or selection, print the selected configuration file as stored, preserving its TOML syntax and comments. The default scope is the project configuration.
.IP
.B --list
prints recognized dotted configuration keys only. It does not print configured values.
.IP
.B get KEY
prints one effective value and its source. The
.B --get KEY
form is also supported.
.IP
.B set KEY TOML_VALUE
sets a key in the selected scope. TOML values must use valid TOML syntax. Strings require quotes, booleans use
.B true
or
.B false,
and arrays use square brackets.
.IP
.B unset KEY
removes a key from the selected scope. The
.B --unset KEY
form is also supported.
.IP
.B --edit
opens the selected configuration file using
.B VISUAL
or
.B EDITOR
or falls back to
.B vi.
.IP
.B --global
selects the user configuration file
.IR ~/.svfconfig .
.B --system
selects
.I /etc/svfconfig
or
.I $PREFIX/etc/svfconfig
when running in Termux.
.IP
.B --verbose
prints the configuration scopes, merged effective settings, precedence, and the source scope of each value. 
.B --debug
adds diagnostic tracebacks when operations fail.
.SH CONFIGURATION KEYS
Configuration uses TOML tables and dotted keys. The recognized keys and their meanings are listed below. Use
.B config --list
to print the recognized dotted keys.
.SS project
.TP
.B project.name
Optional project name used in reports.
.TP
.B project.description
Optional project description.
.SS version
.TP
.B version.initial
Initial semantic version recorded during initialization. Must be a valid SemVer value.
.TP
.B version.source
Inline table identifying the canonical version source. Required fields are
.B type
and
.B file
with optional
.B key
for structured formats. Supported types: text, json, toml, yaml, shell, debian, and debian-changelog.
.SS git
.TP
.B git.tag_prefix
Prefix used when interpreting version tags, commonly
.B v
or an empty string.
.TP
.B git.baseline
Optional commit or tag boundary used when no valid release tag exists.
.TP
.B git.require_clean
When true, require a clean working tree before version-changing operations.
.TP
.B git.unknown_commit
Policy for unrecognized commit types. The default is
.B ignore.
.TP
.B git.merge_commits
Reserved merge-commit policy setting. Current history traversal uses Git's default log behavior.
.SS commits
.TP
.B commits.breaking_changes
Whether recognized breaking-change markers trigger a MAJOR increment.
.TP
.B commits.ignored_types
Array of commit types that do not trigger a version increment.
.TP
.B commits.unknown
Policy for unrecognized commit types, normally
.B ignore.
.TP
.B commits.types.TYPE
Maps a Conventional Commit type to
.BR major ,
.BR minor ,
or
.BR patch .
Defaults include feat=minor and fix/perf/revert=patch.
.SS sync
.TP
.B sync.targets
Array of inline tables identifying version fields to synchronize. Each target requires
.B type
and
.B file
and may include
.B key
for structured formats. Supported target types are text, json, toml, yaml, shell, debian, and debian-changelog.
.SH CONFIGURATION SCOPES
Configuration is merged in increasing precedence:
.IP 1. 4
System: /etc/svfconfig, or $PREFIX/etc/svfconfig in Termux.
.IP 2. 4
User: ~/.svfconfig.
.IP 3. 4
Project: .semver-forge.toml (preferred) or semver-forge.toml (legacy).
.PP
Higher-precedence values override lower-precedence values. Nested tables merge recursively. Arrays such as
.B sync.targets
are replaced by the higher-precedence scope, not concatenated.
.SH VERSION SOURCE FORMATS
.TP
.B text
The entire file contains the version.
.TP
.B json
A JSON value selected by a dotted key; defaults to
.B version.
.TP
.B toml
A TOML value selected by a dotted key; defaults to
.B project.version.
.TP
.B yaml
A YAML value selected by a dotted key; defaults to
.B version.
.TP
.B shell
A single shell-style variable assignment; defaults to
.B VERSION.
.TP
.B debian
The unique
.B Version:
field in a Debian control file.
.TP
.B debian-changelog
The version in the first standard Debian changelog header.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
semver-forge init
semver-forge init --yes
semver-forge check
semver-forge check --verbose
semver-forge check --debug
semver-forge next --dry-run --explain
semver-forge sync --dry-run
semver-forge sync --discover
semver-forge config
semver-forge config --list
semver-forge config get commits.types.feat
semver-forge config set commits.types.feat '"minor"'
semver-forge config unset git.baseline
semver-forge config --global
semver-forge config --system --edit
semver-forge config --verbose
.fi
.SH FILES
.TP
.I .semver-forge.toml
Project configuration, canonical version source, synchronization targets, commit rules, and processed Git history boundary.
.TP
.I ~/.svfconfig
User configuration.
.TP
.I /etc/svfconfig
System configuration; in Termux use $PREFIX/etc/svfconfig.
.TP
.I VERSION
Default canonical version file for projects without an existing recognized authority.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Zero indicates success. A nonzero status indicates invalid configuration, unavailable project data, failed synchronization, or another operation error.
.SH REQUIREMENTS
Python 3.10 or later. Git is required for commit-history-based version selection.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR git (1),
.BR python3 (1)
